  identity: "one_type_variable_bound_to_two_distinct_coproducts" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one type variable is bound by two actuals of distinct types (variants of two different coproducts, or Int and Bool) and the program is Accepted.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: a non-generic f(a: P) called with Q1 is refused (TypeMismatch Coproduct(P) vs Coproduct(Q)). Constructor expressions already elaborate to the owner coproduct. The hole was generic rebind, not variant-to-coproduct typing.",

    "HARM: silent wrongness (DESIGN section 5 / section 4b values inhabit declared types). Two inhabitants of unrelated coproducts share one type variable.",

    "CLIMBED ON THE V1 .dag AUTHORITY. v1.compiler.infer unify_generics returns UnifyGenericsAcc and refuses a later actual that node_type_equals rejects, with a located TypeMismatch naming the generic and both types. First-wins is gone on that authority. Uninformative and self-binding of T complete; they are not a join of two concretes.",

    "RUNG HONESTY: the executing seed still returns a subst map and refuses only via generic_rebind_refusal_diags on a bare formal at the call-arg pass. Nested List<T>, callable, borrowed, and record-lit rebinds can still first-wins in the built binary. EXECUTED RUNG on the seed is therefore 2 for the top-level same_arm REDs only, not 3 for the whole unify. CEILING: 3. NEXT TRIGGER: fleet regen installs UnifyGenericsAcc so the seed is the .dag emit; nested_list_int_vs_bool_is_refused and record Box {1} vs Box {true} refuse on that binary.",

    "RESIDUAL, NOT THIS CLIMB: ConstructorTag<P> {} == ConstructorTag<Q> {} is still Accepted (test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate phantom_constructor_tag_equality_is_observed). That is operator follow-up C, not a green control of this class. NEXT TRIGGER for C: a typecheck refusal of that equality (or a declared reason it is a different class).",

    "EVIDENCE THAT SURVIVES THE CLIMB (DESIGN section 4b(4)): test.claim.cross_coproduct_generic_locate same_arm_cross_coproduct_is_refused (P1, Q1) and same_arm_int_bool_is_refused (1, true); controls same_arm_same_coproduct_is_accepted (P1, P2) and same_arm_int_int_is_accepted (1, 2). Also enrolled on the rust compile path as v1-compiler-tests cross_coproduct_generic_locate_test. The polarity-red constructor_tag_route_probe_red probes and their explicit_witness_admission rows are deleted: they were not a typecheck-refusal control.",
  ],

  evidence: [
